1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:06,041
Welcome to a walkthrough of the GTBIT Student Management ERP, our minor

2
00:00:06,091 --> 00:00:10,476
project at Guru Tegh Bahadur Institute of Technology.

3
00:00:10,526 --> 00:00:16,501
It is one web application that runs the academic and administrative life

4
00:00:16,551 --> 00:00:23,698
of the college, for four kinds of user: administrators, faculty, students and parents.

5
00:00:23,748 --> 00:00:27,882
In the next ten minutes we will sign in as each of

6
00:00:27,932 --> 00:00:36,752
them, and look at every major module, from attendance and examinations to fees, placements and governance.

7
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,355
Here is how it is built.

8
00:00:39,405 --> 00:00:45,789
A React 19 single page application talks to an Express 5 REST API on Node.js.

9
00:00:45,839 --> 00:00:51,972
Every request carries a signed token, is checked against a role permission

10
00:00:52,022 --> 00:00:58,156
matrix, and then passes through one record level scoping rule, so students

11
00:00:58,206 --> 00:01:05,509
see only themselves, parents only their wards, and faculty only the sections they teach.

12
00:01:05,559 --> 00:01:11,692
Data lives in MongoDB Atlas, in thirty seven collections, seeded with nine

13
00:01:11,742 --> 00:01:20,716
hundred and five students, twenty faculty, and more than twenty seven thousand attendance records and marks.

14
00:01:20,766 --> 00:01:28,069
A Python worker runs the CGPA forecasting engine, with an identical JavaScript fallback.

15
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:31,676
Everyone signs in on the same page.

16
00:01:31,726 --> 00:01:36,830
You can use an email, a roll number, an enrolment number, or

17
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:42,586
a faculty employee ID, and the form recognises which one you typed.

18
00:01:42,636 --> 00:01:48,685
Failed attempts are rate limited, and there are no back-door endpoints.

19
00:01:48,735 --> 00:01:51,691
Let's sign in as the administrator.

20
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:58,890
The administrator's dashboard leads with one plain statement: nine hundred and five

21
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:05,172
students are enrolled, and those under the seventy five percent attendance rule

22
00:02:05,222 --> 00:02:07,478
are counted right next to it.

23
00:02:07,528 --> 00:02:13,681
Below are campus attendance, fee recovery, and the early warning cohort, which

24
00:02:13,731 --> 00:02:18,770
lists the students most at risk, with predicted risk by section.

25
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:22,825
Every module is one tap away in the dock, or in the

26
00:02:22,875 --> 00:02:29,664
full screen menu, and the command palette, opened with Ctrl+K, jumps anywhere by name.

27
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:37,582
The student directory filters all nine hundred and five students by semester and section.

28
00:02:37,632 --> 00:02:44,658
Opening a student shows their dossier: identity, guardian, and an attendance snapshot.

29
00:02:44,708 --> 00:02:46,304
Admissions are real.

30
00:02:46,354 --> 00:02:52,885
Admitting a student creates their login with a unique temporary password, raises

31
00:02:52,935 --> 00:02:58,562
the semester's fee invoice, and can create a linked guardian account.

32
00:02:58,612 --> 00:03:02,347
A whole batch can be imported from a CSV file.

33
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:09,451
In examinations, the marksheet shows each semester's grades and SGPA on the

34
00:03:09,501 --> 00:03:12,225
official GGSIPU ten point scale.

35
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:16,645
The exam calendar shows which results are declared.

36
00:03:16,695 --> 00:03:22,539
Faculty can enter marks only for the sections they teach, within the

37
00:03:22,589 --> 00:03:26,093
limits of twenty five, fifteen and sixty.

38
00:03:26,143 --> 00:03:33,287
Publishing an end term result recomputes every affected CGPA, notifies students and

39
00:03:33,337 --> 00:03:37,708
guardians, and recalibrates the forecasting engine.

40
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:44,687
The fee ledger shows demand, collections and overdue amounts for every programme.

41
00:03:44,737 --> 00:03:49,725
Invoices turn overdue after the due date and accrue a late fine,

42
00:03:49,775 --> 00:03:53,819
capped at twenty percent, unless accounts waives it.

43
00:03:53,869 --> 00:03:59,408
Part payments are accepted, every payment is logged with its method and

44
00:03:59,458 --> 00:04:03,266
reference, and receipts are numbered in sequence.

45
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:08,170
Placements show statistics computed from real offers.

46
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:13,199
Each drive has a minimum CGPA and a deadline that are enforced

47
00:04:13,249 --> 00:04:20,906
when students apply, and the placement office moves applicants through shortlisting, interviews

48
00:04:20,956 --> 00:04:24,394
and selection, notifying them at each step.

49
00:04:24,444 --> 00:04:29,911
The library enforces stock, a four book limit and overdue fines, and

50
00:04:29,961 --> 00:04:33,967
hostel allocation keeps room occupancy consistent.

51
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:37,814
Governance is where policy lives as data.

52
00:04:37,864 --> 00:04:43,986
The attendance threshold, the grading scale, the late fee, and the forecasting

53
00:04:44,036 --> 00:04:47,863
model's weights and calibration are all settings.

54
00:04:47,913 --> 00:04:54,193
Every change is validated, applied across the system within seconds, and written

55
00:04:54,243 --> 00:04:57,912
to the audit trail with its old and new values.

56
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:00,334
Now the faculty portal.

57
00:05:00,384 --> 00:05:06,204
A teacher's dashboard shows today's lectures and the students in their own

58
00:05:06,254 --> 00:05:09,694
sections who are under seventy five percent.

59
00:05:09,744 --> 00:05:12,946
The flagship feature is smart attendance.

60
00:05:12,996 --> 00:05:18,736
The teacher picks a mapped class and opens a fifteen minute QR roll call.

61
00:05:18,786 --> 00:05:22,781
The code under the QR changes every thirty seconds.

62
00:05:22,831 --> 00:05:27,699
It is derived from a secret session token and the current time

63
00:05:27,749 --> 00:05:33,886
window, so a photo forwarded to a group chat stops working almost immediately.

64
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:41,264
On the student's phone, scanning the QR opens the portal straight at the check in screen.

65
00:05:41,314 --> 00:05:45,298
Here we type the code shown on the projector instead.

66
00:05:45,348 --> 00:05:50,626
The server accepts the current or the previous window, checks that the

67
00:05:50,676 --> 00:05:54,888
student belongs to this section, and marks them present.

68
00:05:54,938 --> 00:06:00,521
Back on the teacher's screen, the roster updates live, showing the student

69
00:06:00,571 --> 00:06:02,043
as checked in by QR.

70
00:06:02,093 --> 00:06:05,544
Closing the roll call stops further check ins.

71
00:06:06,190 --> 00:06:09,354
Let's sign in as a student, Tejassveer.

72
00:06:09,404 --> 00:06:15,536
His dashboard opens with his attendance in plain words: eighty six percent,

73
00:06:15,586 --> 00:06:20,563
exam eligible, but one subject is under seventy five percent.

74
00:06:20,613 --> 00:06:26,415
The attendance ledger shows every subject against the rule, and for any

75
00:06:26,465 --> 00:06:32,266
shortfall it says exactly how many consecutive classes will recover it.

76
00:06:32,316 --> 00:06:38,283
The same message arrives as an alert, for the student and their guardian.

77
00:06:38,930 --> 00:06:41,927
This is the CGPA probability module.

78
00:06:41,977 --> 00:06:48,698
Before results are declared, it forecasts this semester's SGPA and the resulting

79
00:06:48,748 --> 00:06:52,845
CGPA, with a likely range and a confidence level.

80
00:06:52,895 --> 00:06:58,516
For Tejassveer it predicts an SGPA of eight point eight three, with

81
00:06:58,566 --> 00:07:04,187
high confidence, and flags Software Engineering for low attendance.

82
00:07:04,237 --> 00:07:13,243
Each subject's final mark is projected from internal marks, assignments, attendance and subject difficulty.

83
00:07:13,293 --> 00:07:18,152
In the what if simulator, he can drag a subject higher and

84
00:07:18,202 --> 00:07:21,199
watch the forecast change instantly.

85
00:07:21,249 --> 00:07:22,638
Nothing is saved.

86
00:07:23,290 --> 00:07:25,478
Coursework is fully working.

87
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:31,794
Students upload their submissions as real files, faculty grade them against the

88
00:07:31,844 --> 00:07:36,271
maximum marks, and lecture notes are shared per subject.

89
00:07:36,321 --> 00:07:42,826
The study planner suggests weekly hours for each subject from attendance, internal

90
00:07:42,876 --> 00:07:45,944
marks and difficulty, and explains why.

91
00:07:45,994 --> 00:07:49,461
The career guide builds on declared results.

92
00:07:50,110 --> 00:07:52,703
Compare an at risk student, Aman.

93
00:07:52,753 --> 00:07:59,831
His dashboard warns that he is under the seventy five percent rule and could be detained.

94
00:07:59,881 --> 00:08:06,158
His forecast has moderate confidence, a wider range, and three subjects flagged

95
00:08:06,208 --> 00:08:10,483
for low attendance, each with a reason in plain words.

96
00:08:10,533 --> 00:08:16,650
This is exactly the early, explained warning the system was designed to give.

97
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:20,179
Parents see only their linked wards.

98
00:08:20,229 --> 00:08:26,931
The parent portal shows the ward's attendance, latest marks, notices for guardians,

99
00:08:26,981 --> 00:08:32,463
and fees with the full payment history, so families no longer depend

100
00:08:32,513 --> 00:08:35,554
on the student to pass information on.

101
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:38,079
How good is the forecast?

102
00:08:38,129 --> 00:08:42,786
We back tested it on seven hundred and forty one students and

103
00:08:42,836 --> 00:08:50,271
three thousand seven hundred and five declared subject results, cross validated across semesters.

104
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:55,209
At first the engine was about six marks too pessimistic, and its

105
00:08:55,259 --> 00:08:59,993
bands caught the real mark only forty one percent of the time.

106
00:09:00,043 --> 00:09:05,317
So we made it calibrate itself on the college's own declared results,

107
00:09:05,367 --> 00:09:10,796
with a least squares fit and a band chosen for eighty percent coverage.

108
00:09:10,846 --> 00:09:15,502
Out of sample, the average error fell from eight point one to

109
00:09:15,552 --> 00:09:20,364
six point four marks, eighty one percent of real marks now fall

110
00:09:20,414 --> 00:09:25,765
inside the band, and higher confidence really does mean smaller error.

111
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:30,814
Every screen also works in a dark theme, and on a phone,

112
00:09:30,864 --> 00:09:36,449
where the navigation dock and every module adapt to the smaller screen.

113
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:42,403
To sum up: one secure system for the whole college, record level

114
00:09:42,453 --> 00:09:49,344
access control enforced on every endpoint, rotating QR attendance with live rosters

115
00:09:49,394 --> 00:09:54,948
and recovery alerts, and an honest, self calibrating CGPA forecast.

116
00:09:54,998 --> 00:10:00,467
All twenty eight role boundary tests pass, and the whole cohort is

117
00:10:00,517 --> 00:10:03,645
scored in about a quarter of a second.

118
00:10:03,695 --> 00:10:05,569
Thank you for watching.

